  "readmeFile": "nuget_readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.2.0\n\n* Added: SFtpClient.Rename and RenameAsync rename (move) a remote file or directory, through\n  SSH.NET's RenameFile and RenameFileAsync. On most servers they fail when the new path already\n  exists, as SFTP's rename does. Like the other methods, they connect when needed and disconnect\n  afterwards unless KeepConnectionOpen is true.\n* Updated: the dependency floors move to the latest .NET 10 servicing release, 10.0.13:\n  Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions and System.IO.Hashing on every target, and\n  Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces, System.Formats.Asn1 and Microsoft.Bcl.Cryptography on\n  netstandard2.0. SSH.NET stays at 2026.0.0, its latest release.\n\n10.1.1 fixed Exists and ExistsAsync for a missing path:\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H.Net.Ssh/10.1.1#releasenotes-body-tab\n\nUpgrading from 10.0.x or 2.x? 10.1.0 merged the netstandard2.0 and net8.0+ packages into one and\nraised the dependency floors (including SSH.NET 2026.0.0). Its notes list every change:\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H.Net.Ssh/10.1.0#releasenotes-body-tab",
